<title>CHINA: AIRBUS DELIVERS FIRST A320 TO PHILIPPINES.</title>
<headline>AIRBUS DELIVERS FIRST A320 TO PHILIPPINES.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Airlines (PAL) has taken delivery of its first Airbus A320 and third Airbus type in just over two months, Airbus Industrie said.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, the first of eight Airbus A330-300s arrived in Manila to join the first six of an eventual eight Airbus A340-200/300s.</p>
<p>The intensive refleeting programme will eventually see 12 A320s delivered and PAL is the first airline to operate all three aircraft together which should allow it to significantly reduce operating costs, the statement said.</p>
<p>Airbus Industrie is a consortium made up of French state-owned Ste Nationale Industrielle Aerospatiale, British Aerospace Plc, Daimler-Benz, a unit of Daimler-Benz AG and Construcciones Aeronauticas SA (CASA) of Spain.</p>
